# This file travels with the mirror, which is the point.
#
# The mirror is pushed to github.com/ModelPiper/toolpiper with `rsync --delete`,
# and rsync copies what is ON DISK rather than what git tracks. The monorepo's
# own .gitignore sits at the monorepo root, does not travel, and therefore
# protects nothing on the far side. Without this file a push carries every
# build artefact into a public repository whose commits the Claude plugin
# marketplace pins by SHA, and git history makes that permanent.
#
# Measured 2026-09-05 before the first push: 3,643 files on disk against 24
# tracked, the difference being desktop-extension/node_modules (28 MB) and a
# 2.1 MB built .mcpb.

# npm install output
node_modules/

# Built bundles: scripts/build-mcpb.sh writes dist/toolpiper-<version>.mcpb,
# which ships as a GitHub Release asset, never as a tracked file.
dist/

# Python build and byte-code output for the integration packages
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
build/

.DS_Store
